description:
See or change your own conversation history (only yours). Each message has a line number from 1. The step in progress (the message that called this tool, and after) cannot be changed; everything before it can. Removed messages are kept in a file next to the history. Changes work from your next turn. One op per call:
- list: {"op": "ls"}  (one line per message: LINE, ROLE, TEXT; add "range": "3-8" for some lines)
- delete lines 2 to 5: {"op": "rm", "range": "2-5"}
- replace lines 2 to 5 with a short summary: {"op": "summarize", "range": "2-5", "text": "Earlier: the user asked for the time; it was 10:00."}
- replace line 3 with a whole new message: {"op": "set", "line": 3, "message": {"role": "user", "content": "What time is it?"}}
A range is "N", "A-B" or "A-" (A to the end). Use ls first to see the line numbers. Errors: ArgumentsBad, OpUnknown, RangeBad, MessageBad, HistoryMissing, WriteFailed, DaemonMissing, DaemonFailed, InstanceMissing.
Details: memory me.json#/self_history.
